---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Custom Website Design &amp; Development | Kelp Agency"
  description="Kelp designs and develops custom websites that explain your business, convert visitors, and connect with the systems your team relies on."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Content Creation Services"
    title="Website Design & Development"
    description="Our web design and development team can help you increase sales by providing optimized sites that convert visitors into lifelong customers."
    lottieFile="web-design.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Why design & development matter</h2>
      <p>
        Your website is more than a digital presence—it is a system that
        supports how your business communicates, builds trust, and drives
        action.
      </p>
      <p>
        Effective websites are not defined by design alone. Structure, content,
        performance, and usability must work together to guide visitors toward
        clear outcomes. When those elements are misaligned, even visually strong
        sites underperform.
      </p>
      <p>
        We approach every project with intention—ensuring your site is easy to
        navigate, built for real user behavior, and aligned with your business
        goals.
      </p>
      <h2>Web applications</h2>
      <p>
        Some businesses require more than a marketing website. When your
        operations, data, or customer experience demand it, custom web
        applications provide the flexibility and control that off-the-shelf
        tools cannot.
      </p>
      <p>
        We design and develop web-based tools that streamline processes, surface
        meaningful data, and create more interactive user experiences—all within
        a system that is built specifically for how your business operates.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Custom Website Development</li>
        <li>Web Applications & Internal Tools</li>
        <li>Dashboards & Data Interfaces</li>
        <li>Interactive Data Visualizations</li>
        <li>UI/UX Enhancements & Motion</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Start with the Questions Your Customers Ask</h2>
      <p>
        We map what visitors need to know, where they hesitate, and what your
        team needs the site to accomplish. That work informs the navigation,
        page structure, content, visual direction, and calls to action. A
        service business may need a clearer path from problem to enquiry. A
        complex organization may need several audiences to find different
        information without getting lost.
      </p>
      <h2>Build the Experience and the System Behind It</h2>
      <p>
        Our work can include custom page templates, CMS architecture, accessible
        interfaces, performance improvements, forms, booking paths, dashboards,
        and integrations. If a form needs to create a record in HubSpot, a
        product selector needs to pass specifications to production, or several
        platforms need to feel like one experience, we design that handoff into
        the project. We choose the platform and approach for the problem,
        whether that is WordPress, HubSpot, Shopify, WooCommerce, or a custom
        application.
      </p>
      <h2>Make the Site Easier to Find and Understand</h2>
      <p>
        Useful page copy, internal links, crawl access, and appropriate
        structured data help search systems interpret a site. Google says its
        existing SEO fundamentals also apply to AI features; there is no special
        markup that guarantees an AI mention. We build for people first, then
        make the content technically accessible to search and AI discovery. A
        free <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a> scan can show where
        your current site needs attention before you plan a rebuild.
      </p>
      <h2>See What Specific Development Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        For <a href="/work/us-labels/">US Labels</a>, Kelp refreshed the brand and rebuilt a custom label
        buying experience, then connected WooCommerce to Windows printing
        software through a dedicated API service. For <a href="/work/artisan-talent/">Artisan Talent</a>, the work
        joined a custom WordPress setup, an Angular jobs application, and
        HubSpot pages into a consistent experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your site has outgrown its template or its internal workarounds, tell
        us what customers and staff need it to do. We will help define the right
        scope before the first page is designed.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Discovery, content architecture, and page planning</li>
        <li>Custom design and responsive development</li>
        <li>Forms, applications, and system integrations where required</li>
        <li>Launch review, measurement, and editor handoff</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        A useful first meeting includes your current site, the tasks customers
        struggle with, and the workflows staff have built around it. We can
        separate quick fixes from the work that needs a new architecture.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>How long does a custom website take?</h3>
      <p>
        Timing depends on content, approvals, complexity, and integrations. We
        scope those dependencies before proposing a schedule rather than
        treating every site as the same build.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Let's Talk
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={66} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
